# Findings retired by fingerprint, in the form commit:file:rule:line.
#
# CI scans the full history (fetch-depth: 0), so fixing the working tree does not
# clear a finding - the commit that introduced it is still published. This file
# is how a reviewed non-secret is retired without rewriting history.
#
# Every entry must say what the string actually is and why it is not a secret.
# An entry without that is indistinguishable from suppressing a real leak.

# A test literal, not a credential. TestSecretTravelsOnlyInTheEnvironment asserts
# that a passphrase reaches ssh-keygen through the environment and never through
# argv, so it needs a value it can find again in the child's environ. The
# original was high-entropy and sat next to an identifier called `secret` - the
# exact shape generic-api-key exists to catch, and a fair hit on a fake. The
# working tree now uses THE-TEST-VALUE; this retires the published commit.
